KPL/MYB

Time scales of the IAU and IERS conventions
===========================================

myb knows no time scale by name: a scale is a node of a tree whose root is a
realised atomic scale, and every other scale is defined by its relation to a
parent. This kernel defines the conventional scales; a user may add others.

Relation kinds (X is the scale being defined, FROM its parent; times in seconds
since J2000.0 of the scale concerned, i.e. JD 2451545.0 on that scale):

   OFFSET        X    = FROM + OFFSET
   RATE          X    = FROM - RATE * (FROM - T0) + OFFSET        T0 on FROM
   RATE_INVERSE  FROM = X    - RATE * (X    - T0) + OFFSET        T0 on X
   SERIES        X    = FROM + S(X)    (S: series kernel named by _SERIES; solved
                                        by fixed-point iteration, |dS/dX| < 1e-9)

T0 is given as a two-part Julian date (_T0_JD) so that it is exact.

Definitions
-----------

   TAI   International Atomic Time: root of the tree.

   TT    Terrestrial Time.  TT = TAI + 32.184 s.
         IAU 1991 Resolution A4 (Recommendation IV); IAU 2000 Resolution B1.9.

   TCG   Geocentric Coordinate Time (time coordinate of the GCRS).
         TT = TCG - L_G (TCG - T0),  L_G = 6.969290134e-10 (defining constant),
         T0 = 1977-01-01T00:00:32.184 TCG = JD 2443144.5003725.
         IAU 2000 Resolution B1.9.

   TDB   Barycentric Dynamical Time.  Defined from TCB (below); its relation to
         TT is the relativistic TCB-TCG transformation, represented here by the
         Fairhead & Bretagnon series (kernel tdb-tt-fb1990.tk, accuracy a few ns
         over 1950-2050). An ephemeris-based relation will replace it in module rel.

   TCB   Barycentric Coordinate Time (time coordinate of the BCRS).
         TDB = TCB - L_B (TCB - T0) + TDB0,  L_B = 1.550519768e-8,
         TDB0 = -6.55e-5 s,  T0 = JD 2443144.5003725 TCB.
         IAU 2006 Resolution B3.

   GPS   GPS system time, nominally TAI - 19 s (GPS time started on
         1980-01-06T00:00:00 UTC, when TAI - UTC was 19 s; IS-GPS-200).
   GST   Galileo System Time, nominally aligned with GPS time: TAI - 19 s.
   BDT   BeiDou Time, started on 2006-01-01T00:00:00 UTC when TAI - UTC was
         33 s: TAI - 33 s.
         The GNSS times are nominal: their realisations differ from TAI - n s by
         nanoseconds, published by the system operators and the BIPM (Circular T).

UTC is not a scale of this tree: it labels TAI with leap seconds and is defined by
the table of kernel utc-tai.tk.

\begindata

   MYB_TIME_SCALES = ( 'TAI' 'TT' 'TCG' 'TDB' 'TCB' 'GPS' 'GST' 'BDT' )

   MYB_TIME_TT_FROM    = 'TAI'
   MYB_TIME_TT_KIND    = 'OFFSET'
   MYB_TIME_TT_OFFSET  = 32.184

   MYB_TIME_TCG_FROM   = 'TT'
   MYB_TIME_TCG_KIND   = 'RATE_INVERSE'
   MYB_TIME_TCG_RATE   = 6.969290134e-10
   MYB_TIME_TCG_T0_JD  = ( 2443144.5  0.0003725 )
   MYB_TIME_TCG_OFFSET = 0.0

   MYB_TIME_TDB_FROM   = 'TT'
   MYB_TIME_TDB_KIND   = 'SERIES'
   MYB_TIME_TDB_SERIES = 'TDB_TT'

   MYB_TIME_TCB_FROM   = 'TDB'
   MYB_TIME_TCB_KIND   = 'RATE_INVERSE'
   MYB_TIME_TCB_RATE   = 1.550519768e-8
   MYB_TIME_TCB_T0_JD  = ( 2443144.5  0.0003725 )
   MYB_TIME_TCB_OFFSET = -6.55e-5

   MYB_TIME_GPS_FROM   = 'TAI'
   MYB_TIME_GPS_KIND   = 'OFFSET'
   MYB_TIME_GPS_OFFSET = -19.0

   MYB_TIME_GST_FROM   = 'TAI'
   MYB_TIME_GST_KIND   = 'OFFSET'
   MYB_TIME_GST_OFFSET = -19.0

   MYB_TIME_BDT_FROM   = 'TAI'
   MYB_TIME_BDT_KIND   = 'OFFSET'
   MYB_TIME_BDT_OFFSET = -33.0

\begintext
